# Optional, build-time only. The site works fine without any of these.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in as needed (never commit real values).

# Google Tag Manager container ID. GTM owns all tags, GA4 included —
# the app only pushes events to the dataLayer. Leave unset to use the
# production container (GTM-T5HS9CSJ); set only to build against another one.
VITE_GTM_ID=GTM-T5HS9CSJ

# Legacy: GA4 measurement ID. No longer read by the app — GA4 is
# configured inside the GTM workspace. Kept here for reference only.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# PostHog (DRAFT wiring — org "Newton & Carter", project 700301).
# Leave VITE_POSTHOG_KEY unset and PostHog is a complete no-op.
# The project key is a public key (it ships in the client bundle), but it
# is NOT committed to this repo: Chris copies it from the PostHog project
# settings (Project Settings → Project API Key) into .env.local for local
# builds, or into the Vercel project's Production/Preview env vars.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Optional: ingestion host. Defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=
